                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="538-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="538-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="538-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ><img id="538-3" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ><img id="538-4" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_wc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Wide Cardioid" title="Wide Cardioid" ></span>Oktava MK-012-USB</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The MK-012-USB combines the FET preamp circuit of the famous <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Oktava/MK-012">MK-012</a> with USB power and an A/D converter (16Bit/48kHz resolution). The mic preamp is compatible with most Oktava capsules; see below for a full list.</p><p>The 012-USB ships in a soft case with a USB cable. No capsules are included; the product appears to be targeted at MK-012 owners who seek the convenience of USB-powered recording, and who already own a selection of applicable capsules.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Oktava/MK-012-USB">Oktava MK-012-USB</a> is also known as: MK012 USB.</p><p>The mic was released in 2008.</p>
